WEBVTT

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.430
Randall. Thank goodness.
What are we gonna do about the child?

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:14.510
Shh.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.630
Shh, shh, shh.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.630
(SLAMS)

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.230
It's on the front page.
The child. The one you were after.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:41.630
Be quiet. Don't you think
I'm aware of the situation?

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:43.830
I was up all night trying to find it.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:48.030
I did a calculation factoring in
the size of the sushi restaurant.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.670
The child may have escaped!

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.550
Until we know for sure
we're gonna act like nothing happened.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.990
Get the machine running.
I'll take care of the kid.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:59.350
When I find whoever let it out,
they're dead.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.990
Why are you still here?
Come on, go! Move! Now!

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.270
FUNGUS: I'm not here.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:08.510
SULLEY: (WHISPERING) They're gone.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:12.350
BOO: Ew.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.270
MIKE: This is bad, so very bad.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.670
What were they talking about,
machine?

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:18.190
Who cares?

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:21.590
All we have to do
is call her door and send her home.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:24.390
Right. We're just two regular Joes
on our way to work.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:26.070
We will blend right in.

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:28.990
-Top of the morning.
-What's shakin', bacon?

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.310
Did you lose weight?
Or a limb?

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.870
-You have her card key, right?
-Of course.

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:36.670
I told you I'd get her card key.
I went and got it.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:38.710
Now I have her card key.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:41.150
OK. Here we go.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.830
Take care of yourself. Try not to
run through any more closets.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:52.390
-Mike, that's not her door.
-Of course it's her door.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.030
No. Her door was white
and it had flowers on it.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:58.150
It must have been dark last night
because this is its door.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:01:59.230
(POLKA MUSIC PLAYING)

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:02.030
Hey, you hear that?
Sounds like fun in there.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:05.150
Send me a postcard, kid.
That's Mike Wazowski, care of

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:07.550
22 Mike Wazowski,
you-got-your-life-back Lane.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:10.950
Very good. Now bon voyage.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.910
Bye-bye. Look at the stick.
See the stick? Go get the stick.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:18.350
-Go fetch.
-Mike, this isn't Boo's door.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.070
-Boo? What's Boo?
-That's what I decided to call her.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.190
There a problem?

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.750
Sulley, you're not supposed to name it.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:27.630
Once you name it,
you start getting attached to it.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:31.350
Now put that thing back
where it came from, or so help me...

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:39.790
Hey. We're rehearsing a scene for
the upcoming company play called...

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.430
Put That Thing Back
Where It Came From or So Help Me.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:44.590
It's a musical.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.590
♪ Put that thing back
where it came from or so help me

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:48.950
♪ So help me, so help me ♪

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.110
And cut.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:54.110
We're still working on it.
It's in progress, but we need ushers.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:58.350
Sulley, I've had enough.
Say goodbye to... Where did it go?

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.950
-Where is she?
-She got away from you again?

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:05.590
Well, that is just...
Wait a minute. The sun is coming up.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.270
This is perfect.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:08.710
She's gone!

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:09.870
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.710
Where are you going?
Sulley, don't blow this.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.590
We're so close to breaking the record.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.350
Somebody will find the kid.
It'll be their problem.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:17.990
She's out of our hair!

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.510
-What are you two doing?
-They're rehearsing a play.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.190
♪ She's out of our hair ♪

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:29.190
Can it! So, what do you think
of that kid getting out, Sullivan?

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.470
-Pretty crazy?
-Oh, yeah, crazy.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:34.190
Word is the kid's been traced
to this factory.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.830
-You haven't seen anything?
-Well...

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.830
No. No way.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:43.150
But if it was an inside job,
I'd put my money on Waxford.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:45.190
-Waxford?
-The one at station six.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:48.110
-He's got them shifty eyes.
-Hey, Waxford.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:50.830
-Sulley!
-CELIA: Michael Wazowski!

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:58.270
Last night was one of the worst nights
of my entire life, bar none!

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:03.110
-I thought you cared about me.
-Honey, please.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:06.350
-I thought you liked sushi.
-Sushi! Sushi!

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.190
You think this is about sushi?

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:15.910
Wazowski.

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.470
Michael!

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:18.510
Men.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.870
Breathe. Keep breathing.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.190
(PANTING)

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:35.430
-Where's the kid?
-Kid?

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:38.670
-What kid?
-It's here in the factory, isn't it?

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:43.430
It never would have gotten out
if you hadn't been cheating last night.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.990
Cheating? Cheating. Right.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.510
OK. I think I know
how to make this all go away.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:54.710
What happens when the whistle blows
in five minutes?

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:59.190
-I get a timeout?
-Everyone goes to lunch.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:03.590
Which means the scare floor will be...

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.950
-Painted?
-Empty.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:09.110
It'll be empty, you idiot.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.790
You see that clock?

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:15.190
When the big hand is pointing up
and the little hand is pointing up,

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.750
the kid's door will be in my station.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:20.830
But when the big hand points down,

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:22.910
the door will be gone.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:26.110
You have until then to put the kid back.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:28.430
Get the picture?

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:31.510
(ROARING PLAYFULLY)

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:40.790
Boo!

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:43.790
-No.
-Hey, you. Halt.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.350
He's the one.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:47.950
-The one from the commercial.
-That's him.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:51.510
-Can we get an autograph?
-Oh, sure. No problem.

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:53.950
Make that out to Stephanie,
my daughter.

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:55.190
Yes. Let's see.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.790
"From your scary friend.
Best wishes..."

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:03.030
So, then I said, "If you talk to me
like that again, we're through".

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:05.990
-What'd she say?
-You know my mom.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.870
-She sent me to my room.
-See you guys later. Take it easy.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.310
Bottoms up.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:14.670
(GASPS IN HORROR)

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:28.830
Boo!

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.190
(SINGING)

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:34.990
Hi.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.390
Well, hello, there.
What's your name?

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:41.350
Mike Wazowski.

